terms and users' personal content are excluded.

"Derivative Work" means a modification, translation, adaptation, or combined
work incorporating copyright-protected portions of the Material. Independent
works merely distributed alongside it, or using it through an unmodified public
interface without incorporating protected portions, are not Derivative Works.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for making modifications to
the covered work, including covered source code, editable assets, and the build
and installation instructions and scripts necessary to reproduce that work.
It does not require disclosure of users' private records, photos, credentials,
or independently licensed general-purpose tools and third-party dependencies.
Identify such dependencies and how to obtain them under their own terms.

