4. Professional-use exception

You may use the Material or a Derivative Work as a communication aid in paid
teaching, therapy, care, accessibility support, or similar professional
sessions, including work by self-employed practitioners and for-profit centers.
You may charge for those human professional services. This exception also
permits the necessary internal installation and customization of the aid.

This does not permit charging for the software, installation, software access,
software functionality, or a software license, separately or bundled with those
services. It does not permit distributing a commercial software product or
running a paid software service under the description of professional sessions.
Distribution or network provision of a Derivative Work remains subject to
section 5. Ordinary local use during a session does not itself require publishing
private records or private internal modifications.

5. Attribution, source availability, and same terms

When distributing the Material or any Derivative Work in source or executable
form, or providing users with remote access to its functionality over a network:

a. Include this license and all applicable copyright and third-party notices.
   Clearly identify your modifications and do not suggest endorsement by the
   original author. Do not represent a modified edition as the original edition.

b. Provide the complete Corresponding Source for the covered version, including
   your modifications, to the public at no charge under this same license.
   Provide a clear source link or source archive with every distribution and
   in the interface of any remotely provided edition. Keep source available
   for as long as you distribute or remotely provide that version, and for at
   least three years after the last such distribution or provision.

c. Offer your copyrightable contributions to a Derivative Work under this same
   license and impose no additional contractual, technical, or access restrictions
   on the rights it grants. Recipients must have the same rights to modify and
   redistribute the covered work, subject to the same commercial restrictions.
   This requirement applies to the covered combined Derivative Work, not to
   independent works or third-party components under their own licenses.

Private modifications that are neither distributed nor remotely provided to
others do not require publication. User data is not Corresponding Source.

